  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Turn GC×GC retention times (t1, t2) from a published or recalibrated instrument program into source-traced estimates of 51 physicochemical, environmental-fate, biological-partitioning and sensory/toxicity properties, then explore them as contour maps, peak maps and biological-system views, and check calibration quality and applicability before export. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
